					<description><![CDATA[An SSTV event on the ISS is scheduled to begin on Thursday October 22, 2026 around 15:10 UTC and will end on Monday October 26, 2026 at 17:45 UTC. The ARISS Series 34 images are about ARISS Hardware. The SSTV transmissions will be made using the amateur radio station in the ISS Service Module. The &#8230; &#8230; <a href="https://amsat-uk.org/2026/10/20/iss-slow-scan-tv-oct-22-26/">Continue reading <span class="meta-nav">&#8594;</span></a>]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<div dir="ltr">
<div data-shortcode="caption" id="attachment_36195" style="width: 310px" class="wp-caption alignright"><a href="https://amsat-uk.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/international-space-station-image-credit-nasa.webp"><img aria-describedby="caption-attachment-36195" data-attachment-id="36195" data-permalink="https://amsat-uk.org/2025/07/02/amateur-radio-satellites-in-tes-magazine/international-space-station-image-credit-nasa/" data-orig-file="https://amsat-uk.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/international-space-station-image-credit-nasa.webp" data-orig-size="1368,740" data-comments-opened="0" data-image-title="International Space Station &amp;#8211; Image credit NASA" data-image-description="&lt;p&gt;International Space Station &amp;#8211; Image credit NASA&lt;/p&gt;
" data-image-caption="&lt;p&gt;International Space Station &amp;#8211; Image credit NASA&lt;/p&gt;
" data-large-file="https://amsat-uk.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/international-space-station-image-credit-nasa.webp?w=584" class="size-medium wp-image-36195" src="https://amsat-uk.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/international-space-station-image-credit-nasa.webp?w=300" alt="International Space Station - Image credit NASA" width="300" height="162" srcset="https://amsat-uk.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/international-space-station-image-credit-nasa.webp?w=300 300w, https://amsat-uk.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/international-space-station-image-credit-nasa.webp?w=600 600w, https://amsat-uk.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/international-space-station-image-credit-nasa.webp?w=150 150w" sizes="(max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px" /></a><p id="caption-attachment-36195" class="wp-caption-text">International Space Station &#8211; Image credit NASA</p></div>
<p>An SSTV event on the ISS is scheduled to begin on Thursday October 22, 2026 around 15:10 UTC and will end on Monday October 26, 2026 at 17:45 UTC.</p>
<p>The ARISS Series 34 images are about ARISS Hardware.</p>
<p>The SSTV transmissions will be made using the amateur radio station in the ISS Service Module. The transmission frequency will be 437.550 MHz FM, (+/- 10 kHz Doppler shift) using SSTV mode Robot 36, 36 seconds on with 2 minutes off gap. The ISS callsign will be RS0ISS.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
